WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.460
UNICEF launched the GOBI Campaign to improve child health.

2.1
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:11.560
We need to identify the strategies encouraged by the GOBI Campaign.

3.1
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:18.620
The GOBI Campaign aimed to reduce child mortality through practical interventions.

4.1
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:26.620
The campaign focused on growth monitoring, oral rehydration, breastfeeding, and immunization.

5.1
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:34.330
choice Aincludes continuous evaluation, which is not a primary focus of the GOBI Campaign.

6.1
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:41.420
choice Ddoes not include growth monitoring, a key component of the GOBI Campaign.

7.1
00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:48.650
The correct answer includes growth charts, oral rehydration, and immunization.

8.1
00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:54.710
Immunization is a crucial aspect of preventing childhood diseases.

9.1
00:00:54.710 --> 00:01:02.590
The mnemonic GOBI stands for Growth, Oral rehydration, Breastfeeding, and Immunization.

10.1
00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:09.650
When answering similar questions, focus on the key components of the GOBI Campaign.

11.1
00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:16.310
The GOBI Campaign is a UNICEF initiative aimed at improving child health.

12.1
00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:24.860
The GOBI Campaign focuses on growth monitoring, oral rehydration, breastfeeding, and immunization.
